// A parenthesised expression. Go's composite-literal restriction is SYNTACTIC and applies
// only to a BARE literal in an if/for/switch header: 'if (T{1}) == (T{2}) {' is legal Go
// while 'if T{1} == T{2} {' is not, and likewise 'switch (T1{}) {'. So the group lifts the
// gate for what is inside it and puts it back on the way out. A group that fails after its
// '(' leaves its marker behind; CondOff pops down to its OWN marker so that such a leak
// cannot outlive the header it happened in.
ParenGroup  <~~ push(goParenC(takeAll(), up.pos)) ~~>
