// DOUBLE: 9223372036854775807 comes back as 9223372036854776000 and
// 18446744073709551615 as 18446744073709552000. Both are ordinary Go literals, so
// the value is read exactly instead (parseRadix answers a sized-integer box when
// the digits do not fit a double).
GoDecLit    <~~ push(goRadixLitC(up.in, up.pos)) ~~>
