// before CompLitNI, whose CompName is `Id { "." Id }` and whose SkipBlock would eat
// the body.
//
// THE PEG QUESTION (manual chapter 4). A rule that can match a PREFIX of a later
// alternative must exclude the continuation explicitly. This one cannot: it REQUIRES a
// '.' and a second Id and a '{', so on any input a later alternative would take it
// fails before consuming anything the later alternative wants - `pkga.Fn(` fails at the
// '(', `pkga` alone fails at the missing '.', and the chain form `x.y.z` fails at the
